    "body": "@slouken This does indeed seem to be the problem.\r\nhttps://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/011502711603074fef225134ec1b44b36e3b5c9e/src/joystick/controller_list.h#L601\r\nSDL itself is reporting the Steam Deck as VID = `0x28de`, PID = `0x11ff`, which matches \r\nhttps://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/011502711603074fef225134ec1b44b36e3b5c9e/src/joystick/controller_list.h#L597\r\nthe unknown steam virtual gamepad. Is this a Steam input interference?\r\n\r\nYou could say there is nothing you can do here, but then what is the point of the deck driver, if it can never even be used?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
