    "updated_at": "2024-03-24T07:15:54Z",
    "body": "When I developed the HIDAPI SteamDeck driver, I used a SteamDeck running ArchLinux and the AntiMicroX input mapper to access the controller over SDL2. The mapped input was used to play some non-steam games. But the `testcontroller` tool from SDL3 shows the gyro and accelerometer values fine for me as well.\r\n\r\n~~Since Linux allows only one application to open a hidraw device~~ (Edit: It actually allows it)~~, I think a problem could be the running Steam client which already opens the hidraw device as part of SteamInput~~.\r\nPlease also note that there is a quirk in the SteamDeck kernel driver that hides the classic gamepad device as soon as the hidraw device is opened (see https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/hid/hid-steam.c).\r\nAs an overall result, only the Steam virtual gamepad may be present and accessible.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
