    "updated_at": "2024-03-24T07:37:50Z",
    "body": "I found out that it is actually possible to open a hidraw device by multiple applications simultaneously on Linux. I corrected my above comment.\r\nAlso, with the current SDL3 version (675c9f01ff391e559cb9f76a8cc621884b2ff1a5) I was able to successfully run both, the SDL2 `testgamecontroller` and the SDL3 `testcontroller`, apps simultaneously on the hidraw SteamDeck driver and they both received valid input.\r\n\r\nHowever, replacing `testgamecontroller` with a real SDL2 app like `wine control` or `antimicrox` does not work. It disconnects the input from the test app.\r\n\r\nEdit: This issue only happens on my SteamDeck. I cannot reproduce it with the DualSense hidraw driver on a PC. There, `testcontroller`, `testgamecontroller`, `wine control` and `antimicrox` are running together without any issue.",
