    "updated_at": "2024-03-27T18:12:11Z",
    "body": "For the use case with the steam client, I added a sysfs switch to my [prototype kernel driver](https://github.com/mmmaisel/linux/blob/steam-deck-gyro-6.8/drivers/hid/hid-steam.c) that allows to override the exclusive access quirk.\r\nThis worked in first tests when using the kernel driver to access the device with SDL3 (SDL2 does not support the kernel sensors interface as far as I know).\r\n\r\nAlso, upstream Linux 6.8 changed that you have to press and hold the top left \"options\" button for a short moment, until it beeps, to enable the controller at all.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
